 with a phone once (flickos-phone pair). It speaks only the part of KDE
 Connect's protocol that moving things, ringing, the battery,
 browsing the phone's files and the choices below need. The phone's
 notifications can be shown here too, for the apps you allow and never
 while the screen is locked
 (flickos-phone set notifications yes); that is off until turned on.
 The phone's calls can be shown too: who is calling, with Mute, and what
 is playing pauses until the call ends (flickos-phone set calls yes).
 That is off until turned on, and nothing is shown while the screen is
 locked.
 The phone can control what's playing here too, and sees its name and picture
 (flickos-phone set media yes). That is off until turned on, and it
 changes nothing while the screen is locked.
 The phone can run commands named on this computer: it is sent only the
 names (flickos-phone commands add NAME COMMAND). The list is empty
 until one is added, and nothing runs while the screen is locked.
 It listens only on the networks where a phone was paired, and nothing
 runs while it is off.

